    "description": "Beat-by-beat outline (Save the Cat / Hero's Journey / Story Circle / Kishōtenketsu / Seven-Point).",
    "group": "craft",
    "id": "STRUCTURE",
    "name": "Structure Outline",
    "prompt": "You are a story architect. Produce a complete chapter-by-chapter OUTLINE for "The Test Book" before any prose is written.

Premise: A premise worth testing
Genre: thriller
Chapters: 6 · ~3000 words each · english

═══ CHOOSE A STRUCTURE (pick the best fit, or let the user specify) ═══
• Save the Cat! — 15 beats (Opening Image → Catalyst → Midpoint → All Is Lost → Finale)
• Hero's Journey — 12 stages (Call → Mentor → Ordeal → Return with Elixir)
• Story Circle — 8 steps (You / Need / Go / Search / Find / Take / Return / Change)
• Kishōtenketsu — 4 acts, conflict-optional, built on a recontextualizing twist (great for literary, slice-of-life, kids)
• Seven-Point — built backward from the ending (Hook, Plot Turns, Pinch Points, Midpoint, Resolution)

═══ OUTPUT ═══
1. State the chosen structure and why it fits this premise.
2. Map every beat to a chapter number (1-6) with a 1-2 sentence purpose.
3. Mark the inciting incident, midpoint, and climax chapters.
4. For each chapter: a one-line "promise" (what the reader gets) and a hook for the chapter end.

FORMAT: output one line per chapter as "N. <beat>" (e.g. "1. ...", "2. ...") so it can be pasted into the Outline field and auto-mapped to each chapter prompt.",
